      "formation": "22nd Division (Funck), VII Corps (Reynier)",
      "side": "Saxon",
      "summary": "Left alone at Kobrin to watch the Mukhavets crossings while Reynier's corps was strung out to the west, the brigade found Russian columns closing on every road. It barricaded the town and fought all day from its houses and the old fort, until, with the town burning and its ammunition spent, Klengel surrendered with some 2,300 men.",
      "notes": [
