    {
      "id": "kobrin-tormasov",
      "nationId": "russia",
      "name": "Tormasov's Columns",
      "formation": "Third Army of the West",
      "side": "Russian",
      "summary": "Tormasov, coming north from Volhynia, closed on Kobrin from three sides at once: Madatov's hussars from the north on the Pruzhany road, the Pavlograd Hussars and 13th Jäger from the west, and dragoons and two Jäger regiments from the south. They cut the Saxons off and pressed into the town street by street until it surrendered.",
      "notes": [
        "After Nafziger, who gives the troops by the road they came on: from the north the Alexandria Hussars (four squadrons, in two waves), the Starodub Dragoons and Tatar Uhlans; from the west the Pavlograd Hussars (eight squadrons, so Large) and the 13th Jäger; from the south the Starodub and Tver Dragoons and the 10th and 14th Jäger. A Cossack sotnia with Madatov is left out.",
        "Single squadrons make the Tatar Uhlans and the Tver Dragoons (two squadrons) Small. Nafziger doesn't give every regiment's battalions; two field battalions each are shown, the usual for 1812.",
        "Nafziger names no guns; Tormasov's batteries shelled the town, so add a Light Battery to the Jäger if you like.",
